# Testing Rules

## TDD Workflow (CRITICAL)

1. **RED** — Write failing test first
2. **GREEN** — Minimum code to pass
3. **REFACTOR** — Clean up, keep green

## Test Structure

```
src/__tests__/
  setup.ts                 # Global setup
  helpers/
    auth.ts                # createMockSession(), createAuthMock()
    db.ts                  # Test database utilities
  unit/                    # Pure function tests (Vitest)
  integration/             # API route handler tests (Vitest)
e2e/                       # Browser flow tests (Playwright)
```

## Test Conventions

- Tests MUST exercise real code paths, not mock variables
- Mock ONLY boundaries (auth sessions, external APIs)
- NEVER mock the function/route under test
- Test names describe behavior: "returns 401 when not authenticated"
- Each test verifies ONE behavior
- Use helpers from `src/__tests__/helpers/`

## Commands

```bash
npm run test           # Vitest (unit + integration)
npm run test:watch     # Watch mode for TDD
npm run test:e2e       # Playwright E2E
npm run test:all       # Everything
```

## Anti-Patterns

❌ `expect(true).toBe(true)` — tests nothing
❌ Mocking the subject under test
❌ Test names with "and" (split into two tests)
❌ Skipping the RED step
❌ Writing implementation before tests
